)PANEL KEYLIST(ISRHELP,ISR)
)ATTR DEFAULT(%+_)
/*********************************************************************/
/* PANEL    : MBKGLSH                                                */
/* TITLE    : HELP - GL SUSPENSE CLEARING                            */
/*-------------------------------------------------------------------*/
/* 2008-06-23 KLM  ORIGINAL                                          */
/*********************************************************************/
  % TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE) SKIP(ON)
  + TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN) SKIP(ON)
  ] TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) SKIP(ON)
)BODY EXPAND(//) WIDTH(80)
%TUTORIAL -/-/- GL SUSPENSE CLEARING -/-/- TUTORIAL
%Command ===>_ZCMD                                                             +
+
+Postings the GL feed cannot map (unknown product, missing GL code, out of
+balance batch) are raised as suspense items in MBK.GLSUSP and posted to
+the suspense GL.  Finance Operations investigate them in Oracle GL and
+then tell the mainframe the item is cleared, so that it drops off the
+ageing report.
+
]Actions+
+  %C+Cleared - a manual journal (MJnnnnnnnn) has moved the amount to the
+      right GL in Oracle.  No approval needed.
+  %W+Write off - the amount is written off to the suspense write-off GL.
+      Needs a second user (four eyes) and is limited to 500.00 by
+      GLSUS010.  Use the WO form reference or the journal number.
+
]Ageing+
+   0-5 days normal, 6-30 watch, 31-90 escalated to the Finance Controller
+   nightly, over 90 days reported to Internal Audit (GLSUS01 ends RC 4).
+
]Cut-off+
+   Release from option R before 21:30 for tonight's GLSUS01.
+   If DB2 is unavailable the item cannot be checked - you may still key
+   the instruction; GLSUS010 rejects it overnight if it is wrong.
)PROC
  &ZUP = MBKMENUH
)END
